# Imported maps, and the Python bytecode of the importer.
#
# `maps/imported/<id>/` is DERIVED: tools/bsp_import.py regenerates all of it from
# the .bsp in one pass of about four seconds, so committing it buys nothing and costs
# 14 MB for two maps. The stronger reason is that those bytes are somebody else's map.
# Reading a third-party .bsp for its dimensions and its ramp angles is what
# godot/inspirations/ is for, in the shape godot/../external-study/ already has;
# redistributing its geometry in this repository is a different act and wants the
# author's permission. The generated <id>.gd and <id>.tscn live INSIDE that directory
# rather than beside the hand-written maps, so this stays one line and never becomes a
# list of map names to keep in step -- which is this tree's most repeated bug.
/maps/imported/
/tools/__pycache__/
screenshots/
/addons/dot_spectate
/addons/dot_effects
